From 09471c0bd202ef93aa8be0f94dd62fe8ee37bb01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:12:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): quarantine only deterministic conflicts;
 per-receipt holds; release = acceptance + certified catch-up [daveey]

Review round 3 of #3796 (both 0e97d5a6fd reviews plus the second reviewer's findings).

- Only a ContainmentConflict (identity_changed in remember, event_differs in certify_page) quarantines; any
  other ContainmentRefused (non-live/unproven evidence, unavailable proof, invalid page) re-raises so #3759's
  per-board backoff retries the page with the cursor unmoved. A transient evidence failure is never a hold.
- Hold rows are keyed (task_id, receipt_uid, via): a task stays held while any unreleased receipt names it,
  directly or as a dependency; a release removes only that receipt's rows.
- Release (hermes kanban sync quarantine --release R --reason TEXT) fetches the Board's current evidence and
  refuses unless it is live and certifies; appends a containment_sync_acceptances row (sha256 of the certified
  identity, evidence, reason, operator, time) that remember() honours while the first receipt stays; replays the
  receipt's canonical event and the withheld rows it frees through certify_page + apply_remote_changes, and
  lifts the holds inside that apply transaction. CLI runs replica first, then live, under board_sync_lock.
- One hub card per quarantined receipt via the hermes-hub courier (idempotency key
  containment-quarantine:<board>:<receipt>), ERROR log only on the hub, 10 min courier backoff; held cards get a
  sync_quarantine queue reason and a refusal naming the receipt and the release command.
- A held task's own chat-link/attachment deletes wait (owner recorded by a host-local delete trigger);
  adopt copies only new hold/acceptance rows and never the withheld ledger; CLI exit codes 0/1/2 tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
